sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-bressloff-audit-v2-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants — Code-to-model traceability: 68/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "The main modelling functions carry equation/figure references in their docstrings (local W_n to Eq. 3.12, lateral W_n^lat to Eq. 4.9, dispersion to Section 4 / Figs 16-17, gamma_2 to Eq. 5.14, gamma_3 to Eq. 5.15 / Figs 37-40, the map to Section 2 / 2002 Eq. 2.1) and the figure panels are labelled by paper figure. Deductions: the branch-selection machinery (`_make_branch_candidate` score, lattice-local scope, even-hex stability shortcut, clipping guards) has no source reference and is not in the paper (-10); `planform_modes` amplitudes, phase scales (0.35, -0.25, 0.5) and the hex_pi/triangle sign patterns are given without pointing to the planform definitions of Section 5 (-8); the `spec_to_preset` mapping that ties fixture figure IDs (fig37-fig40) to presets named after other figures (fig17, fig35, fig16, fig36) is unexplained (-6); the contoured rendering and tanh sharpness are rendering heuristics inherited from upstream with no paper anchor (-5); the alpha/beta map constants lack a derivation comment (-3). Evidence: 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L462–L469: branch_growth docstring ties the dispersion relation to Section 4 and Figs 16-17 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L462-L469>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L516–L539: gamma_2 / gamma_3 docstrings cite Eqs 5.14-5.15 and Figs 37-40 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L516-L539>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L759–L790: planform_modes amplitudes/phase scales with no equation reference <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L759-L790>; 2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py L955–L961: Unexplained fixture-id to preset-id mapping used for the parity check <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/9b18c52/2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py#L955-L961>." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.68"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-bressloff-v1-form-constants-code-traceability> rdfs:label "Bressloff et al. (2001/2002) V1 Euclidean Symmetry-Breaking & Klüver Form Constants (2001-bressloff-v1-form-constants.py, docs/media/bressloff_v1_form_constants.gif, bressloff_v1_metrics.csv, datasets/bressloff/horton_hoyt_1991_magnification.json) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Code-to-model traceability' for Homo sapiens primary visual cortex (V1) — geometric visual hallucinations (Klüver form constants) and flicker phosphenes" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (primary) + Gemini 4 Argon (independent blinded second assessor)" .
}

